    [BugFix] Preserve GLM shared slots with layerwise KV transfer (#19880)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Fix GLM-5.3-Flash Model Runner V2 initialization with Memcache
    `use_layerwise: true`. GLM's planner already overlays MLA/KDA and
    indexer/tail caches across scheduler groups, but the generic V2
    allocation loop mistakes their zero-stride descriptors for cross-layer
    scratch aliases and raises `Layerwise V2 KV aliases require identical
    cache specs.`
    
    Allocate GLM-Next descriptors in a dedicated path before generic
    hybrid/scratch dispatch. Validate descriptor geometry and layer
    coverage, allocate one aligned backing per physical slot, map its
    members to that backing, and return. This follows the review suggestion
    and removes the two GLM exemptions from the generic path. Existing
    reshape code builds the per-spec views; other models retain scratch-spec
    validation, and actual Mamba cross-layer scratch reuse remains
    unsupported. The change affects initialization only.
    
    Duplicate-work check: searched open PRs for GLM/layerwise, the exception
    text, MRV2, and alias keywords, and inspected the related diffs. #16858
    and #16946 address Memcache transfer lifecycle, #18172 addresses GLM
    PP/MTP allocation, and #19494 addresses the shared-pool capacity budget;
    none contains this scratch-alias classification fix.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    N/A.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Enable kvpool with layerwise, startup succeed:
    
